        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/f04885/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-11-30T18:23:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>if proletariat uses duplicate, then overwhelm, can he use the overwhelm to us duplicate again? Despite it not being unlimited? Also, what if beacon were to allow proletariat to use overwhelming duplicate with bolstering team up, after he had used duplicate on his own turn already? Would that work? And finally, is it possible for legacy to use motivational charge on an allied proletariat, hitting him, and thus making a clone due to the card proletariat has that reduces damage to one and makes a clone, and then proletariat is healed by motivational charge resolving, so that proletariat effectively gets a free clone? And if beacon moves, then does bolstering team up, can she use her bolstering team up action to move again?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:52.134Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
