      {
        "id": 151027,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-11-30T19:07:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"evren2\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/f04885/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> evren2:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>if proletariat uses duplicate, then overwhelm, can he use the overwhelm to us duplicate again? Despite it not being unlimited?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, Overwhelm allows you to choose any action. &nbsp; This would result in a total of four Proletariats on the board after those two actions.</p>\n<blockquote></blockquote>\n<p>Also, what if beacon were to allow proletariat to use overwhelming duplicate with bolstering team up, after he had used duplicate on his own turn already? Would that work?</p>\n<p>yes, it's a new turn and this would be allowed &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<blockquote></blockquote>\n<p>And finally, is it possible for legacy to use motivational charge on an allied proletariat, hitting him, and thus making a clone due to the card proletariat has that reduces damage to one and makes a clone, and then proletariat is healed by motivational charge resolving, so that proletariat effectively gets a free clone?</p>\n<p>You have to choose the order to work that way but yes this is possible &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<blockquote></blockquote>\n<p>And if beacon moves, then does bolstering team up, can she use her bolstering team up action to move again?</p>\n<p>I believe Beacon would have to choose a different action</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:29:46.851Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 13919,
        "topic_slug": "getting-additional-action-uses",
        "display_username": "Sonvar",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"evren2\"]\n\nif proletariat uses duplicate, then overwhelm, can he use the overwhelm to us duplicate again? Despite it not being unlimited?\n\n \n[/quote]\n \n\n Yes, Overwhelm allows you to choose any action. &nbsp; This would result in a total of four Proletariats on the board after those two actions. \n\n \n>  \n\nAlso, what if beacon were to allow proletariat to use overwhelming duplicate with bolstering team up, after he had used duplicate on his own turn already? Would that work?\n\n \n \n\n yes, it&#39;s a new turn and this would be allowed &nbsp;&nbsp; \n\n \n>  \n\nAnd finally, is it possible for legacy to use motivational charge on an allied proletariat, hitting him, and thus making a clone due to the card proletariat has that reduces damage to one and makes a clone, and then proletariat is healed by motivational charge resolving, so that proletariat effectively gets a free clone?\n\n \n \n\n You have to choose the order to work that way but yes this is possible &nbsp;&nbsp; \n\n \n>  \n\nAnd if beacon moves, then does bolstering team up, can she use her bolstering team up action to move again?\n\nI believe Beacon would have to choose a different action\n",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 5464,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 2,
