      {
        "id": 151029,
        "name": "RySmith6",
        "username": "RySmith6",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rysmith6/{size}/1852_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-24T01:27:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Overwhelm says to select an action, not use it. &nbsp;Each Proletariat takes that action. &nbsp;You are not using the selected action, Overwhelm is giving you the effect of that action for each Proletariat.&nbsp;That is the difference.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This^^<br>This is what I needed to help explain why Tachyon does not get an extra attack when earning an extra sprint from Unrelenting Momentum. The sprint means she may make an active attack, but not take the action associated with the attack. Since the action to make the attack was not spent, Tachyon cannot Sprint-&gt;punch,Sprint-&gt;punch, Free Sprint-&gt;punch, (free punch), unspecified third action. I had such a hard time justifying this.</p>\n<p>I should really start pointing to health actions and passive hazards to help explain how attacks can be separated from actions taken.<br><br>Wow. This also helps explain why a Wraith with Slip into Shadows may sprint twice on her turn, as the Slip into Shadows sprint is not an action taken. Thanks for the concise explanation!</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:29:46.991Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
